<https://imagesnippets.com/imgtag/images/british_library@zeroexp.com/farm6.staticflickr.com%252F5520%252F11275715606_f3f1b3ffa9_c.jpg.html>
        <http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml/vocab#stylesheet>
                <https://imagesnippets.com/imgtag/adeel/style.css>;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#description>
                "The ABC Bearings for 1880 Text \"...the bearing points, and this without the removal or addition of a single part. The A B C Bearings for 1880 are applied to the back wheels of Bicycles, and to the hubs of Tricycles. The A B C Bearings for 1880 Are applied to the pedals in a new and original manner. They have no projections, and are always in the right position for mounting. These new Pedals can be supplied...\" Illustration Black and white Section view Technical drawing Cutaway drawing Cyclist Cycling Bicycle  Title: \"The Bicycle Road Book: compiled for the use of bicyclists and pedestrians. Being a ... guide to the roads of England, Scotland, and Wales, etc\" Author: SPENCER, Charles - Professor of Gymnastics Shelfmark: \"British Library HMNTS 10347.bb.3.\" Page: 206 Place of Publishing: London Date of Publishing: 1880 Publisher: Griffith & Farran Issuance: monographic Identifier: 003460101  Note: The colours, contrast and appearance of these illustrations are unlikely to be true to life. They are derived from scanned images that have been enhanced for machine interpretation and have been altered from their originals."@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#image>      "http://farm6.staticflickr.com/5520/11275715606_f3f1b3ffa9_c.jpg"@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#image:alt>  "The ABC Bearings for 1880"@en;
