        <https://ogp.me/ns#description>
                "CP Railway train going through CN Railway rock sheds along the Thompson River near Spences Bridge, BC.  Both Canadian National Railway and Canadian Pacific have tracks on either side of the river.  The two railroads have an agreement for a directional running zone along the valley where eastbound trains use the CP tracks and westbound trains use the CN tracks.  CP 8712    Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
