<http://farm5.staticflickr.com/4112/5016015168_76c346a27a.jpg>
        a                               <https://w3id.org/lio/v1#Image> , <http://schema.org/ImageObject>;
        <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment>
                "Coming out of Chicago, our Amtrak first pulled west over the river, then we up and over the draw bridges to cross back over where we came from to head south.  Below, you can see a metra train pulling in. Beyond the bridge, you can see several trains in the yards. All of this leads to Union Station which is left of the Willis (Sears) Tower.  My personal interest is in the bridge. It's obviously in disuse now, but it used to handle traffic from Chicago's now gone Grand Central Station... including trains from the Chicago Great Western.    Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
        <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso>
                <https://imagesnippets.com/imgtag/rdf/yfcc01@zeroexp.com/farm5.staticflickr.com%2F4112%2F5016015168_76c346a27a.jpg>;
