<https://imagesnippets.com/imgtag/images/yfcc01@zeroexp.com/farm9.staticflickr.com%252F8007%252F7701410998_69ceff1e25.jpg.html>
        <http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml/vocab#stylesheet>
                <https://imagesnippets.com/imgtag/adeel/style.css>;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#description>
                "A series of 150 pictures showing the disused Welsh Highland Railway. The railway alignment in Portmadoc looking in the Dinas/Caernarfon direction. The white rendered house marks the position of the level crossing over Snowdon Street. Just behind the camera position is the point where the revived WHR makes a deviation from the original alignment and follows a new route to Britannia Bridge where it rejoins the old formation.  This section of line reopened to passenger trains in 2011.  OS grid reference: SH570388  5th May 1990.    Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#image>      "http://farm9.staticflickr.com/8007/7701410998_69ceff1e25.jpg"@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#image:alt>  "Welsh Highland Railway - The Wilderness Years #145"@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#title>      "Welsh Highland Railway - The Wilderness Years #145"@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#type>       "website"@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#url>        "https://imgsnp.co/5sg3j"@en;
        <twitter:card>                 "summary_large_image"@en .

