<http://farm2.staticflickr.com/1093/1120947616_83b5dd74e4.jpg>
        a                               <http://schema.org/ImageObject> , <https://w3id.org/lio/v1#Image>;
        <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment>
                "The Tay Rail bridge taking from the wormit side looking towards Dundee, the old supports still seen to the right of the bridge. In 1879 the bridge collapsed when a train was crossing causing the lives of 75 people to be lost. Due to that accident the bridge was rebuilt, however the origional arch supports are still visible as a chilling reminder of the bridges tragic past.    Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
        <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso>
                <https://imagesnippets.com/imgtag/rdf/yfcc01@zeroexp.com/farm2.staticflickr.com%2F1093%2F1120947616_83b5dd74e4.jpg>;
