                "The Pink-backed Pelican (Pelecanus rufescens) is a member of the pelican family of birds. It is a resident breeder in Africa, southern Arabia and apparently extinct in Madagascar in swamps and shallow lakes.The plumage is grey and white, with a pinkish hue on the back. Breeding adults have long feather plumes on the head.    Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
