        <https://ogp.me/ns#description>
                "This sparrowhawk was sat at the bottom of the garden watching the finches on the bird feeders. A pity it was a dull day as trying to hand hold the camera with a telephoto lens really needed a much faster shutter speed. Its nice to have such an impressive bird of prey as a regular visitor to the garden, but I hope it doesn't discourage the finches and tits visiting the feeders.    Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
