        <https://ogp.me/ns#description>
                "Mexican Brown Pelican . (Pelecanus occidentalis). Taken in the marina in Puerto Aventuras, Mexico, on the 28/12/2012 at 10:12:13Hrs (1603GMT) using a Nikon D3100 camera with a Tamron AF70-300mm F4-5.6 Di LD MACRO 1:2 lens. The Brown Pelican is the smallest of the eight species of pelican, although it is a large bird in nearly every other regard and is one of  only two of the pelican species which feeds by diving into the water  Click on IMAGE or press L to view on BLACK. Right click on IMAGE & choose ORIGINAL for more detail.    Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#image>      "http://farm9.staticflickr.com/8360/8437894116_4cf668e965.jpg"@en;
