<http://farm8.staticflickr.com/7157/6421233589_95216f0f81.jpg>
        a                               <http://schema.org/ImageObject> , <https://w3id.org/lio/v1#Image>;
        <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment>
                "I noticed that a rail line was near Chalk Farm / Cadmen / Hampstead. So on the second day in London, I made a minor detor to take photos of this railway bridge and the line below, before returning to get our tube to Central London from Chalk Farm.  I think it is the electrified line into and out of Euston.  Near here was Primrose Hill Station (closed in 1992 - demolished since then).  Train on the far right is 378 207. It is a London Overground train.  Made by Bombardier.  From here you can see the construction site of Shard London Bridge (I would later get close up shots of that).    Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
        <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso>
