<http://farm9.staticflickr.com/8091/8403227262_bee2e956b6.jpg>
        a                               <https://w3id.org/lio/v1#Image> , <http://schema.org/ImageObject>;
        <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment>
                "The trackbed of the former GWR Cheltenham - Honeybourne line  looking towards Lansdown Junction in Cheltenham. The surviving former Midland Railway lines run through the right hand arch of the bridge in the distance and Cheltenham Spa (Lansdown) station is situated off to the right. This picture was taken in the early months of 1986, the camera position being beneath the Queen's Road overbridge on top of a large pile of debris that had recently been cleared from the site of Malvern Road station.    Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
