<http://farm6.staticflickr.com/5263/5640091429_3f1f9e953d.jpg>
        a                               <https://w3id.org/lio/v1#Image> , <http://schema.org/ImageObject>;
        <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment>
                "These bridges, over West Fayette Street, used to carry trains into a railroad yard and roundhouse south of the road. I've never seen a metal deck used before. Odd how the tracks were held down. I'm standing on the western bridge, and  you can just barely see the eastern bridge peeking over.    Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
