        <http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml/vocab#stylesheet>
                <https://imagesnippets.com/imgtag/adeel/style.css>;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#description>
                "Post processing: Not a traditional HDR.  What I did was duplicate the image on a top layer.  In channel mixer I converted to monotone, then cranked the green all the way up and blue all the way down (IR effect). Then I adjusted the opacity of the layer to let in some of the original color (though I still desaturated a little).  There's also some highlight/shadow tool, Gaussian blur (gradient) & a slight vignette. Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#image>      "http://farm1.staticflickr.com/225/470867492_fe4d10d854.jpg"@en;
