<http://farm8.staticflickr.com/7171/6547343135_9ba11c705c.jpg>
        a                               <https://w3id.org/lio/v1#Image> , <http://schema.org/ImageObject>;
        <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment>
                "The Sackets Harbor & Saratoga railroad was to connect both towns (and provide an essential link from the D&H to Lake Ontario and all its ports). It was never finished. Some parts were graded on the west end, and some parts were graded here, but this part was never finished. These two photos are shot from slightly different angles so that you can flip between them and get a sense of how far away things are. The filling has slightly petered out here, but resumes further to the north. It was getting dark and I still had to walk back to my car, so I didn't pursue it.    Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
        <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso>
                <https://imagesnippets.com/imgtag/rdf/yfcc01@zeroexp.com/farm8.staticflickr.com%2F7171%2F6547343135_9ba11c705c.jpg>;
