<https://imagesnippets.com/imgtag/images/yfcc01@zeroexp.com/farm9.staticflickr.com%252F8151%252F7466793500_984078e149.jpg.html>
        <http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml/vocab#stylesheet>
                <https://imagesnippets.com/imgtag/adeel/style.css>;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#description>
                "Went for a family walk to Haley Farm State Park on Wednesday and was able to get a few shots of the osprey couple feeding their chicks. Pretty good sized now too! Looked like a good sized fluke was on the menu. We tried getting a bit closer, but she yelled at us, so we backed up the hill and put on the doublers. This is actually the 400mm f5.6   a stacked 1.4x and 2.x  so effectively it's 1200mm lens? but that's also why it's a bit soft. Really needed the tripod, but the monopod ddi result in a useable shot, so I'm happy!  Not a fluke, finally downloaded the images from the 1D and it's clearly not a flatfish.    Image provided by Yahoo!/Flickr and shared under a Creative Commons license for research purposes only."@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#image>      "http://farm9.staticflickr.com/8151/7466793500_984078e149.jpg"@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#image:alt>  "Feeding Time"@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#title>      "Feeding Time"@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#type>       "website"@en;
        <https://ogp.me/ns#url>        "https://imgsnp.co/6q4zd"@en;
        <twitter:card>                 "summary_large_image"@en .

